<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-10-26T05:00:30Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Serbia's Vucic concedes defeat in historic snap election with record turnout</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3fae3f724ee47ed5dc080e468344e4698f381c8d7f1d5399d96347bdd23222da</id><updated>2026-10-26T05:00:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T21:24:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261025-serbia-s-vucic-concedes-defeat-in-historic-snap-election-with-record-turnout" /><summary type="html">Serbia's Aleksandar Vucic conceded defeat in an historic election on Sunday following a near to 70% turnout at polling stations – the highest since the break-up of Yugoslavia in 1992. The snap election followed nearly two years of student-led demonstrations against perceived corruption and authoritarianism triggered by the deaths of 16 people when a train station canopy collapsed in the ‌city of Novi Sad in 2024.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>The week in pictures: Protests across France, wildfires in Indonesia and Brazilian elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:42d0b81fcafbb2810cd92bc64ec8c154f59785e22e6c8fdb2f66807dca459526</id><updated>2026-10-26T05:00:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T12:48:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261025-the-week-in-pictures-protests-across-france-wildfires-in-indonesia-and-brazilian-elections--3fb12d327891.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261025-the-week-in-pictures-protests-across-france-wildfires-in-indonesia-and-brazilian-elections" /><summary type="html">From student protests across France over the weekend and presidential elections in Brazil pitting leftist incumbent Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva against right-wing challenger Flavio Bolsonaro to wildfires in Indonesia, FRANCE 24 looks back at some of the most striking images from the past week.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Serbia holds parliamentary election as populist leader Vucic faces student movement</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0fd08e5fbf3376d2e84fc03904a27d4e0874f7677c8e6017dcf984835542cb3f</id><updated>2026-10-26T05:00:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T07:14:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261025-serbia-holds-parliamentary-election-as-populist-leader-vucic-faces-student-movement--d43323a472f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261025-serbia-holds-parliamentary-election-as-populist-leader-vucic-faces-student-movement" /><summary type="html">Serbia votes on Sunday in what is set to be its most contested parliamentary election in more than 14 years, as a student-led movement seeks to oust the party of populist leader Aleksandar Vucic. The vote comes after nearly two years of student-led protests sparked by the 2024 collapse of a canopy that killed 16 people.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>“Witkoff should step down” says Ukraine Committee Chief</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ee29a62f59ce449bd4a284963c02b061392237bf1b39a4bd647f033de46f798f</id><updated>2026-10-26T05:00:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T18:37:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261024-witkoff-should-step-down-says-ukraine-committee-chief--c1a0869eb9ff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261024-witkoff-should-step-down-says-ukraine-committee-chief" /><summary type="html">Ukraine’s access to Starlink and Starshield satellite links has been restored to the speeds it had before restrictions that disrupted front-line operations for more than a week, Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy said Saturday.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine says Starlink and Starshield connection 'stable' again</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a1405eb108ba5da119d18cb93bc6845a4f219a001caddabbcce6fee0f2ff66ec</id><updated>2026-10-26T05:00:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T09:48:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261024-ukraine-says-starlink-and-starshield-connection-stable-again--c2932aea6b3d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261024-ukraine-says-starlink-and-starshield-connection-stable-again" /><summary type="html">Ukraine has regained a "stable" connection to the Starlink and Starshield satellite communications systems, Kyiv's defence minister said on Saturday. Recent disruptions to the connection led to tensions with Washington over the SpaceX-made network crucial to the Ukrainian army's operations.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Protests against cost of living expected in Italy under heavy security</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3019cf1c5446cc15b87d0d682fb1eb99e9140932ac9fd44b9f86f0a551e33fa6</id><updated>2026-10-26T05:00:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T07:08:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261024-protests-against-cost-of-living-expected-in-italy-under-heavy-security--6332b0b26bda.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261024-protests-against-cost-of-living-expected-in-italy-under-heavy-security" /><summary type="html">Italy is preparing for another day of protests on Saturday against budget cuts and the high cost of living in eight cities, including Rome and Milan. Following last weekend’s unrest, authorities announced heavy security measures, including the use of drones and helicopters to monitor the marches.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>After French Riots, Curfews &amp; Calm .. is a new Storm Brewing ? Plus Ukraine &amp; Israel</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:851cb24090053e152e7a24819a1e3fabeb49e60474f683b4d8ea293925624b8a</id><updated>2026-10-26T05:00:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T18:48:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20261023-after-french-riots-curfews-calm-is-a-new-storm-brewing-plus-ukraine-israel--493a50160c77.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20261023-after-french-riots-curfews-calm-is-a-new-storm-brewing-plus-ukraine-israel" /><summary type="html">It's been a week that’s seen mass protests hijacked by violent rioters across France. The looting of shops, trashing of public buildings, the burning of Lyon’s Tourist Information and the iconic Limoges City Hall.  After the riots, came the curfews, and the contemplation, who did what and why weren’t they stopped. Seditious groups, ultra left anarchists and opportunist criminals said President Macron, with a qualified mea culpa: failures in anticipation and authorities dropped the ball in intelligence gathering. Macron is out of breath,  exhausted and disorientated claimed the Presidential Frontrunner Marine Le Pen, the far right leader now polling in an even stronger position for the Presidency. Foreign leaders had a free for all too, President Trump wading in and Israel’s prime minister settled old scores ahead of elections there. But France wasn’t isolated in its protests and unrest, Milan was a mirror image, with demonstrations in Spain, Portugal, Belgium too, An Autumn of Discontent, and more protests to follow this weekend:</summary><category term="The World This Week" /></entry><entry><title>Europe faces threat of organised sabotage, terrorist attacks: Estonian FM Tsahkna</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c36333c07487f9140162f696546b095f39899cb5c29d579cffd06c820aeb9b65</id><updated>2026-10-26T05:00:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T14:55:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261023-europe-faces-threat-of-organised-sabotage-terrorist-attacks-estonian-fm-tsahkna--a6e98bafae87.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261023-europe-faces-threat-of-organised-sabotage-terrorist-attacks-estonian-fm-tsahkna" /><summary type="html">Estonia's counterintelligence service has recently warned that sabotage operations orchestrated by Russian special services have reached a new and dangerous phase in Europe, with targets no longer being purely symbolic. Talking Europe sits down with the country's foreign minister, Margus Tsahkna, to discuss the security situation in Estonia and the European Union in general.</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>EU member states wrangle over all-important budget: Is a deal this year feasible?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b45a3582a1e8a1afe7a5bb2754c24f0271f5f6c0f2cb2588170d1c0c812cc4aa</id><updated>2026-10-26T05:00:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T14:45:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261023-eu-member-states-wrangle-over-all-important-budget-is-a-deal-this-year-feasible--1d074336636b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261023-eu-member-states-wrangle-over-all-important-budget-is-a-deal-this-year-feasible" /><summary type="html">A marathon EU summit on October 15-16 failed to produce a breakthrough on the European Union's next long-term budget. Although EU leaders put on a brave face at the end of the talks by saying that "the way forward is clearer", EU capitals appear deadlocked on what that path is. At stake is the EU's ability to finance its strategic priorities from 2028 to 2034. The main dividing line is between the so-called "frugal countries", who want deep cuts to the proposed budget, and the "friends of cohesion", who say that cuts are not the answer.</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>French authorities tighten restrictions and ban specific protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4d3b48450ac8e5bfe681c82bd9b925d2ba4627452e3ec904f70ff49067d3fb52</id><updated>2026-10-26T05:00:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T13:55:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261023-french-authorities-tighten-restrictions-and-ban-specific-protests-1--e47d4eb7e179.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261023-french-authorities-tighten-restrictions-and-ban-specific-protests-1" /><summary type="html">France is bracing for another weekend of protests, after violence erupted on the sidelines of last week's mobilisations. Paris is extending a partial curfew in parts of the city until Monday, while protests are banned altogether in the cities of Marseille and Lyon. 70,000 security personnel will be deployed on Saturday and only union demonstrations will be authorised.</summary></entry><entry><title>Major protests in France: "There is a frustration that has accumulated"</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c94582b865e0c144ea7fcb07d4fc47c2e69e2c2fa47c323a722d4e14dd2a9cb5</id><updated>2026-10-26T05:00:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T13:20:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/major-protests-in-france-macron-convenes-student-representatives--222e3ff88ce4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/major-protests-in-france-macron-convenes-student-representatives" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron is set to meet with high school pupils whose protests over school conditions have sparked a broader movement. Details by Philippe Moreau-Chevrolet, communication specialist and teacher at Sciences Po.</summary></entry><entry><title>REPLAY: Laurent Nunez holds presser on security arrangements ahead of protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:07617e83c7b00cf7f68cbd74a61fdf034aaeb9e3aaa5eb6db68bf10b530f1636</id><updated>2026-10-26T05:00:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T11:29:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/replay-french-interior-minister-holds-presser-on-security-arrangements-ahead-of-protests--93a92335ffc5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/replay-french-interior-minister-holds-presser-on-security-arrangements-ahead-of-protests" /><summary type="html">French Interior Minister Laurent Nunez held a press conference on security arrangements ahead of upcoming protests. He announced that 70,000 security forces would be mobilised on October 24 to keep order.</summary></entry><entry><title>Politics in 'materialist terms': Gen Z in Albania, Italy, France and India protesting for 'fairness'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:74467f0119ae661400ef94f654bcd3c2c8efefd05ea0bb10f42e6fcc0d48fe67</id><updated>2026-10-26T05:00:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T09:04:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/politics-in-materialist-terms-gen-z-in-albania-italy-france-and-india-protesting-for-fairness--feef842897cf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/politics-in-materialist-terms-gen-z-in-albania-italy-france-and-india-protesting-for-fairness" /><summary type="html">Jean-Emile Jammine is pleased to welcome Gökçe Tuncel, Sociologist and post-doctoral researcher associated with the Université Paris-Est Créteil (UPEC). For Tuncel, the wave of youth-led protests across France, Albania, India and Italy reveals more than a succession of localized grievances. It signals the emergence of a political consciousness shaped by material insecurity, institutional disillusionment and an increasingly explicit demand for solidarity and social justice. "What is really striking about this Gen Z movement is how clearly young people see their material conditions," Tuncel observes.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia ready for talks on plans for final Ukraine deal, not truce: Putin</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8501d38479f9c11b42988a796284bea23238ceee2265cb37a86e3e61c0041f69</id><updated>2026-10-26T05:00:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T08:00:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russia-ready-for-talks-on-plans-for-final-ukraine-deal-not-truce-putin--990847eb5355.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russia-ready-for-talks-on-plans-for-final-ukraine-deal-not-truce-putin" /><summary type="html">Russia is ready to resume three-way talks with Ukraine and the United States, but on the security parameters of a final peace d al and not a "short" ceasefire, President Vladimir Putin said Thursday.</summary></entry><entry><title>‘Nothing has changed’: Ukraine says still experiencing Starlink restrictions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ee4c64f061306ea69ab10d31dd50e841f7b4d929c9874a0e63219d23ad8ff9f1</id><updated>2026-10-26T05:00:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T06:22:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261023-us-offers-mixed-messages-on-limits-to-ukraine-s-starshield-system--4047733cea7f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261023-us-offers-mixed-messages-on-limits-to-ukraine-s-starshield-system" /><summary type="html">Ukraine on Friday said it was still experiencing restrictions with the Starlink communication system despite a claim by US President Donald Trump made earlier this week that the country’s access had been fully restored. Trump said he had not yet spoken to SpaceX CEO Elon Musk about the problem, but that he would “straighten it out”.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>French student groups call for protests to continue after meeting with Macron</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3c4dfc541fcb98311a04e53ecc2837c535db28a90f8e5d8d5d66c1ec4f72b3ab</id><updated>2026-10-26T05:00:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T05:06:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261023-macron-meets-with-student-representatives-and-law-enforcement-ahead-of-new-protests--325d4c2058c1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261023-macron-meets-with-student-representatives-and-law-enforcement-ahead-of-new-protests" /><summary type="html">Representatives from French high school student groups called for “continued mobilisation” after meeting with President Emmanuel Macron at the Élysée palace for the first time since protests started more than a month ago. Earlier, Interior Minister Laurent Nunez said some 70,000 security forces would be deployed to keep order throughout France for planned protests on Saturday. Read our blog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'The best on Earth': Can weak economic growth undermine Europe's 'very sophisticated social system'?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7bd79f79bb279c1430b1f7eaafa2b11eb8b373994ae874613d332173a576e305</id><updated>2026-10-26T05:00:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T19:59:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261022-the-best-on-earth-can-weak-economic-growth-undermine-europe-s-very-sophisticated-social-sys--032262c59603.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261022-the-best-on-earth-can-weak-economic-growth-undermine-europe-s-very-sophisticated-social-system" /><summary type="html">Can Europe continue to sustain one of the world's most ambitious social models while falling increasingly behind its major economic competitors? For Pascal Lamy, former European Commissioner for Trade and former Director-General of the World Trade Organization, this question lies at the heart of the continent's mounting economic and political tensions.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Targeted by Trump, International Criminal Court wins top EU rights prize</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6bb61c36c7cda52acfd75556de8cca71f1b1cd07114d39e77dcf30465bf9344b</id><updated>2026-10-26T05:00:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T18:55:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/targeted-by-trump-international-criminal-court-wins-top-eu-rights-prize--47212a333be2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/targeted-by-trump-international-criminal-court-wins-top-eu-rights-prize" /><summary type="html">Facing US sanctions, the International Criminal Court was on Thursday awarded the European Union's top rights prize, in a show of support that risks upsetting President Donald Trump. "The European Union is built on respect for multilateralism and international institutions, and this prize recognises the important work of the court in upholding international law and justice," said European Parliament chief Roberta Metsola in announcing the award. The ICC thanked the European Parliament for giving it the Sakharov Prize "at a time when the Court and its officials face unprecedented challenges". FRANCE 24's International Affairs Commentator Douglas Herbert has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>‘No change’ in Russia’s attitude on war shown by deadly attacks, Zelensky says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3604840ec796477a05c89ef18f20722a3394ff7e03d4f712bdab2324c7003935</id><updated>2026-10-26T05:00:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T16:43:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261022-no-change-russia-attitude-war-after-deadly-attacks-zelensky-says--f6950b28e297.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261022-no-change-russia-attitude-war-after-deadly-attacks-zelensky-says" /><summary type="html">Russia’s latest attacks on Ukraine show there has been “no real change” in Moscow’s attitude towards the war, Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky said Thursday. The deadly strikes came just hours after Russian President Vladimir Putin told US envoy Steve Witkoff his country was ready to resume trilateral talks with Washington and Kyiv.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>French shopkeepers fear new looting in upcoming protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f05d7790d80e719d0597de3bba5d7c670a29c171c13a7be60db3c5086d29a937</id><updated>2026-10-26T05:00:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T15:51:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/french-shopkeepers-fear-new-looting-in-upcoming-protests--1070da488c7e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/french-shopkeepers-fear-new-looting-in-upcoming-protests" /><summary type="html">In Paris, shopkeepers fear further losses ahead of a demonstration planned for next Saturday. After last weekend’s protests saw scenes of vandalism, some are considering closing their shops, while others plan to stay open.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine and Russia exchange strikes after US envoy visit to the Kremlin</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8405eca88ee495f17e6001447688de9e397dd53cc8facd417bfd08788ccb13e3</id><updated>2026-10-26T05:00:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T15:50:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ukraine-and-russia-exchange-strikes-after-us-envoy-visit-to-the-kremlin--2cc9c804ffb1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ukraine-and-russia-exchange-strikes-after-us-envoy-visit-to-the-kremlin" /><summary type="html">Ukraine and Russia exchanged drone and missile strikes on Thursday, killing seven people in Ukraine, according to authorities. Moscow said it had intercepted 630 Ukrainian drones targeting the Russian capital. The strikes came hours after US envoy Steve Witkoff met Vladimir Putin in St. Petersburg. Witkoff said Moscow was ready to resume trilateral talks with Kyiv and Washington.</summary></entry><entry><title>French students demonstrate again, despite school holidays</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c2a640c4d2ba00016ce795e6a4ef6ff2085117a365baf480605c84657f8636c7</id><updated>2026-10-26T05:00:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T15:37:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/french-students-demonstrate-again-despite-school-holidays--bec0c1ce221c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/french-students-demonstrate-again-despite-school-holidays" /><summary type="html">The French "interfac" student movement organised new protests on Thursday, even though it is currently the school holidays in France. Student representatives are set to meet soon with Education Minister Edouard Geffray. Details by FRANCE 24's Ellen Gainsford.</summary></entry><entry><title>Italian truckers block roads to protest against soaring diesel prices</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:270b3aa0274248c381a30b9d343c7d15bf89229bb05e18cbb3242e5731703ad7</id><updated>2026-10-26T05:00:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T15:31:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261022-italian-truckers-block-roads-to-protest-against-soaring-diesel-prices--799010a68224.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261022-italian-truckers-block-roads-to-protest-against-soaring-diesel-prices" /><summary type="html">Italian truck drivers have been blocking refineries and key roads to protest against soaring diesel prices. Italy’s government has warned truckers blocking roads could face criminal penalties, as authorities move to clear demonstrations. Details by FRANCE 24's correspondent in Rome, Seema Gupta.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia agrees to resume trilateral peace talks on Ukraine war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:da8bc2f3612266fd133eefd7d66032ab8ae57552c3764af50d592a6d8ac8bc4c</id><updated>2026-10-26T05:00:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T14:19:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russia-agrees-to-resume-trilateral-peace-talks-on-ukraine-war--3812ad570c67.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russia-agrees-to-resume-trilateral-peace-talks-on-ukraine-war" /><summary type="html">A US envoy met Putin in Saint Petersburg on Wednesday after the Kremlin agreed to resume peace talks with Ukraine and the United States. Details by FRANCE 24's correspondent Gulliver Cragg.</summary></entry><entry><title>International Criminal Court wins EU's Sakharov human rights prize</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:56b4a50633ec0d05a86c348fe9cce27279948613fc3b1ef7af5f881b11df9312</id><updated>2026-10-26T05:00:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T10:10:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261022-international-criminal-court-wins-eu-s-sakharov-human-rights-prize--377ffee036a4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261022-international-criminal-court-wins-eu-s-sakharov-human-rights-prize" /><summary type="html">The International Criminal Court, which US President Donald Trump's administration has threatened to dismantle "brick by brick", has been awarded the European Union's Sakharov human rights prize.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Popular dissatisfaction' across Europe: 'Promises of more economic growth haven't come true'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8b4400021b981fac8b762f6fc215014a741f977e6de2ce9827f82b0625ed879c</id><updated>2026-10-26T05:00:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T09:01:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261022-popular-dissatisfaction-across-europe-promises-of-more-economic-growth-haven-t-come-true-1--e3b1e3a3015b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261022-popular-dissatisfaction-across-europe-promises-of-more-economic-growth-haven-t-come-true-1" /><summary type="html">Oliver Farry is pleased to welcome Steven Erlanger, Chief Diplomatic Correspondent in Europe for The New York Times, based in Berlin. Europe's political centre is confronting a crisis that extends far beyond electoral volatility. From France and Germany to Italy and Spain, mounting economic frustration, generational inequality and declining confidence in established political leadership are reshaping the continent's democratic landscape. "The promises of more economic growth haven't come true," explains Erlanger, describing a continent marked by "a kind of general disgust" and "a sense of drift."</summary></entry><entry><title>Europe's wave of anger: How far will youth-led protests go?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f4334f226f06d79ce869a038fda9b3cb15603a80c2abf92dc82ca60e77a16cf2</id><updated>2026-10-26T05:00:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T08:12:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261022-europe-s-wave-of-anger-how-far-will-youth-led-protests-go--2ac6a7fa712b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261022-europe-s-wave-of-anger-how-far-will-youth-led-protests-go" /><summary type="html">Youth-driven protests have been popping up all over Europe: in Belgium, Italy, Spain, Portugal, Albania, Serbia and Greece. The spark here in France was deteriorating conditions in high schools and universities, particularly for students from underprivileged backgrounds. Meanwhile, wages aren't keeping up with inflation. The housing crisis is front and centre in places like Spain and Portugal, while corruption and democratic backsliding have sparked uproar in Albania and Serbia.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine’s Pavlohrad refuses to yield to Putin despite unrelenting bombardment</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cf41a74ca4a75e5f8a79b739e29628b71702079df5df45bc167cfa962dc08f11</id><updated>2026-10-26T05:00:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T05:54:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261022-war-in-ukraine-under-bombardment-the-city-that-refuses-to-bow-to-putin--9894c7d9df26.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261022-war-in-ukraine-under-bombardment-the-city-that-refuses-to-bow-to-putin" /><summary type="html">In Pavlohrad, a Ukrainian city less than 90km from the front line with Russia, there is no respite from war. Residents describe daily life under bombardment, caught between exhaustion and determination. Amid criticism of Trump, TikTok rumours and strikes against civilians, FRANCE 24 gathered accounts from those who “refuse to yield”.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Authorities in Lyon and Marseille ban all protests Saturday</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e2f5c1af144c78551523fae4272ffcb2a0171ef1a0f79f4cd12ba12e859dd4de</id><updated>2026-10-26T05:00:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T02:28:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261022-live-paris-bans-protests-after-violent-unrest-as-macron-takes-swipe-at-trump--cfffc232b5b9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261022-live-paris-bans-protests-after-violent-unrest-as-macron-takes-swipe-at-trump" /><summary type="html">Local prefects on Thursday banned all protests in France’s second- and third-largest cities Marseille and Lyon for Saturday in an attempt to prevent a repeat of last weekend’s violence and looting on the margins of demonstrations over the cost of living and education funding. Read our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russia and Ukraine trade strikes overnight as Moscow signals readiness for peace talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4fa7a371e56ee497d092a70b242ce43d69f713475d2ac11704a1097d6d0f0fe3</id><updated>2026-10-26T05:00:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T01:51:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261022-russia-missiles-kyiv-ukraine-peace-talks--f80fffbbf2e8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261022-russia-missiles-kyiv-ukraine-peace-talks" /><summary type="html">Russia and Ukraine traded major drone and missile strikes on each other's capitals overnight, hours after Moscow signalled readiness to resume US-mediated peace talks. President Donald Trump said negotiations were closer than ever to ending the war, though the Kremlin expressed doubts over Ukrainian and European proposals.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry></feed>
